'''Sammo''' was an individual that [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva Andor]], a resident of the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]], considered to be family.<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> By [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|102}}</ref> Sammo was one of the few people that Maarva had told that the true [[homeworld]] of her adoptive [[Gender|son]], [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], was the planet [[Kenari]].<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> In that [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Date" /> the [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Preox-Morlana corporation]] put out a warrant for a Kenari male on Ferrix, causing Maarva and Cassian to discuss who else knew about the latter's true origin. Maarva initially claimed everyone that she had told was [[Death|dead]], but when Cassian pointed out that Sammo and Maarva's friend [[Jezzi]] knew, his [[Parent|mother]] dismissed the concern.<ref name="That Would Be Me" />

==Behind the scenes==
Sammo was mentioned in "[[That Would Be Me]]," the second episode of the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'',<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> which aired on [[September 21]], [[2022]].<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|cKOegEuCcfw|Andor &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+ (2:25)|sw_url=video/andor-official-trailer}}</ref>

